<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helsinki Final Act</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1975</span> · Also known as Helsinki Accords</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Helsinki Final Act was signed on 1 August 1975 in Helsinki by 35 states, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and almost all European countries, at the end of the Conference on Security and Co-operation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. It recognised the inviolability of post-war borders and committed the signatories to respect human rights, giving dissidents in the Eastern bloc a basis for their demands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/helsinki-final-act.jpg" alt="Helsinki Final Act" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rabax63 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schlussakte_Helsinki_1975_(KSZE).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
